                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Projects capture a high-level overview of what we need to deliver to our clients, while deliverables track the specifics, such as deadlines, kick-off calls, and analyst assignments. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliverables can be used to track a variety of products, such as memos, briefings, tailored reports and dashboards, access to EG executives, recurring calls, speaking events, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check the &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eurasiagroup.sharepoint.com/sites/External/Client%20contracts%20%20relationship%20management/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FExternal%2FClient%20contracts%20%20relationship%20management%2FStreamline%20deliverables%20with%20projects%20in%20Salesforce%2Epdf&amp;amp;parent=%2Fsites%2FExternal%2FClient%20contracts%20%20relationship%20management&amp;amp;p=true&amp;amp;ga=1&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Streamline deliverables with projects in Salesforce&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; guide to learn how to create Projects and their related Deliverables.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</value>
